The provided code is a set of unit tests for the `VertexAIKernelBuilderExtensions` class, which is part of the `Microsoft.SemanticKernel` namespace. The tests are written using the xUnit testing framework and are designed to verify the behavior of the `AddVertexAIGeminiChatCompletion` method.

The first test, `AddVertexAIGeminiChatCompletion_ServiceProviderGetServiceCalled`, tests that the `GetService` method of the `IServiceProvider` interface is called when the `AddVertexAIGeminiChatCompletion` method is invoked. The test uses a mock implementation of the `IServiceProvider` interface to verify that the `GetService` method is called with the correct arguments.

The second test, `AddVertexAIGeminiChatCompletion_ServiceProviderGetServiceCalled_WithBearerKey`, is similar to the first test but tests the `AddVertexAIGeminiChatCompletion` method with a bearer key instead of a bearer token provider.

To write these tests, you would need to create a test class that contains the two test methods. You would also need to create a mock implementation of the `IServiceProvider` interface using a mocking library such as Moq.

Here is an example of how you might write these tests:
```csharp
using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;
using Microsoft.SemanticKernel;
using Microsoft.SemanticKernel.Connectors.Google;
using Moq;
using Xunit;

namespace Microsoft.SemanticKernel.Tests
{
    public class VertexAIKernelBuilderExtensionsTests
    {
        [Fact]
        public void AddVertexAIGeminiChatCompletion_ServiceProviderGetServiceCalled()
        {
            // Arrange
            var serviceProviderMock = new Mock<IServiceProvider>();
            var loggerFactoryMock = new Mock<ILoggerFactory>();
            serviceProviderMock.Setup(p => p.GetService(It.IsAny<Type>())).Returns(loggerFactoryMock.Object);

            var builder = new KernelBuilder(serviceProviderMock.Object);
            var modelId = "model-id";
            var bearerTokenProvider = () => new ValueTask<string>("bearer-token");
            var location = "location";
            var projectId = "project-id";

            // Act
            builder.AddVertexAIGeminiChatCompletion(modelId, bearerTokenProvider, location, projectId);

            // Assert
            serviceProviderMock.Verify(p => p.GetService(It.IsAny<Type>()), Times.Once);
        }

        [Fact]
        public void AddVertexAIGeminiChatCompletion_ServiceProviderGetServiceCalled_WithBearerKey()
        {
            // Arrange
            var serviceProviderMock = new Mock<IServiceProvider>();
            var loggerFactoryMock = new Mock<ILoggerFactory>();
            serviceProviderMock.Setup(p => p.GetService(It.IsAny<Type>())).Returns(loggerFactoryMock.Object);

            var builder = new KernelBuilder(serviceProviderMock.Object);
            var modelId = "model-id";
            var bearerKey = "bearer-key";
            var location = "location";
            var projectId = "project-id";

            // Act
            builder.AddVertexAIGeminiChatCompletion(modelId, bearerKey, location, projectId);

            // Assert
            serviceProviderMock.Verify(p => p.GetService(It.IsAny<Type>()), Times.Once);
        }
    }
}
```
Note that these tests assume that the `KernelBuilder` class has a constructor that takes an `IServiceProvider` instance as a parameter. You may need to modify the tests to match the actual implementation of the `KernelBuilder` class.
